From 46c6ba0c9c39f49e60f746af8053a5bf5c3467b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xtu-v41 <xtu@local>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 23:18:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/16] fix(DSv4.1/SM80): remove Triton fp8e4nv dependency from
 V4.1 cache/indexer ops

Same class of bug already fixed for DeepSeek-V4: Triton has no fp8e4nv on Ampere
(SM80), so '.to(tl.float8e4nv)' cannot compile on A100.

- cache_utils.py: e4m3 encode/decode via _f32_to_e4m3_uint8 / _e4m3_uint8_to_f32
  (the store/load target is already a uint8 pointer -> byte layout unchanged)
- cache_utils.py: gate the cuTeDSL dequant-gather fast path off on Ampere/Ada
- fused_compress_quant_cache.py: the fp8_ds_mla uint8 paged path (ratio 1/2).
  The FlashInfer-only fp8_e4m3 row path (STORE_FP8) is deliberately NOT changed:
  it is not on the fp8_ds_mla path and its target really is an fp8 pointer.
- indexer_k_store.py: per-token FP8 indexer K store.

Verified bit-exact: a Triton kernel using the helpers reproduces torch's
float8_e4m3fn bytes exactly (0 mismatches in 1M values, decode error 0.0).

(cherry picked from commit cb35809cb61bf1674d32da267a6ab113603bc909)
